        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1790">

                <pb facs="1175" n="1059" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1059"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.001/23.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Persian Chargé Affaires
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Persian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to submit, for
                    your excellency’s information, the translation of a cipher despatch which I have
                    received from Vossoughed Dovleh, the Minister of Foreign Affairs at Teheran. The
                    message follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>On the twenty-seventh £ay of Shaban 1332 (July 1914), in accordance with
                            Article 38 of the Fundamental Law, the coronation of His Imperial
                            Majesty the Shah will take place, and His Majesty will take the reins of
                            the affairs of the Government and the Empire in his own hands. On this
                            day the seventeenth of Rabiol Aval (February 13, 1914), His Highness the
                            Regent will make a formal proclamation to the above effect, which will
                            be communicated to all the provinces as well as to the other countries.
                            Please duly advise the official sources concerning this message. No.
                            529.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mirza Ali Kuli Khan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
